return [
    '/pvc-doors-interiors/' => 'PVC and WPC fit-out materials have become the sensible choice for Nigerian homes, offices, schools and institutions, where humidity, damp and termites quietly destroy conventional timber, MDF and plywood. This department brings together everything you need to finish or refurbish an interior: PVC doors that never warp or swell, wardrobes and storage that shrug off moisture, kitchen cabinetry built for wet, hard-working rooms, decorative wall and ceiling panels, and the boards, sheets, edging and trims that tie a project together. Because PVC and WPC are 100% waterproof, termite-proof and need no painting, they outlast wooden alternatives in Lagos conditions while staying light and quick to install. Explore the subcategories below to go straight to what you need, whether that is a single internal door, a full fitted wardrobe, a marble-effect wall finish or pallets of sheets for a development. OfficeLand supplies all of it in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with professional measurement, fabrication and installation, and we handle complete fit-outs, bulk orders, developers, tenders and government and institutional projects. Tell us what you are building and request a quote; we reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-doors/' => 'PVC doors are moulded from solid or hollow WPC cores that will not warp, swell, crack or rot the way timber and flush plywood doors do once Nigerian humidity and damp set in. That makes them ideal for bathrooms, kitchens, toilets, back passages and any room where water and steam are a daily reality, as well as bedrooms and offices where you simply want a clean, maintenance-free door. They are termite- and borer-proof, wipe clean in seconds and never need sanding or repainting, so a building looks newer for longer. When choosing, think about the core first: solid WPC feels heavier and more solid underfoot and suits busy entrances, while a lighter moulded door works well for internal rooms. Match the door to its frame and architrave, confirm the handing and swing, and specify good hinges and locks. Finishes range from crisp white to convincing wood-grain. OfficeLand supplies PVC doors in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring, fabricating and installing to suit each opening, and we fit out full projects, estates and institutions in bulk. Send us your door schedule and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-doors/internal-doors/' => 'Internal doors separate rooms, control sound and give a home or office its finished feel, so it is worth choosing ones that stay true for years. PVC and WPC internal doors do exactly that, resisting the moisture, damp and heat that leave ordinary wooden doors sticking in their frames or dropping on their hinges during the rainy season. They are completely waterproof, termite-proof and need no painting, which matters in bedrooms, studies, store rooms and corridors throughout Nigerian buildings. When specifying, measure each opening carefully and confirm the door size, the hand and which way it should swing, since internal layouts vary from room to room. Decide between a lighter hollow core for quiet rooms and a solid WPC core where you want a weightier close and better sound reduction. Pick a finish that works across the whole floor, from plain white to warm wood-grain, and set it off with matching frames and quality hinges. OfficeLand supplies internal PVC doors in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with measurement, fabrication and installation included, and we handle apartment blocks, schools and offices in volume. Share your room list and request a quote, and our team will respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-doors/door-frames/' => 'A door is only as good as the frame and architrave that carry it, and this is exactly where traditional timber lets Nigerian buildings down. Wooden frames absorb moisture from blockwork and floors, then swell, split or fall to termites, pulling the whole door out of true. PVC and WPC frames and architraves solve this permanently: they are waterproof, termite-proof and dimensionally stable, so the door keeps swinging freely for years without jamming or dropping. When ordering, the key measurement is the wall thickness, as the frame must wrap the opening cleanly before the architrave is added to cover the joint between frame and wall. Note the door size and handing too, so the frame is rebated on the correct side. Architraves come in matching profiles and finishes, from plain white to wood-grain, giving each doorway a neat, consistent border. Because the components are light, they install quickly and cleanly on site. OfficeLand supplies PVC door frames and architraves in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring and fitting them to each opening, and we supply them in bulk for developers, contractors and institutional jobs. Send us your opening sizes and request a quote; we will get back to you within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-doors/flush-doors/' => 'Flush doors give a smooth, flat face with clean lines that suit modern homes, offices and institutional corridors, and in PVC or WPC they keep that sleek look without the hidden weaknesses of plywood flush doors. Conventional flush doors delaminate, bubble and rot once humidity, leaking roofs or wet cleaning reach their inner core, and termites hollow them from within. A moulded PVC or WPC flush door stays completely waterproof and termite-proof, wipes clean and never needs repainting, so it holds its finish in busy, hard-used spaces. Choosing one comes down to the core and the fit: a solid WPC core gives a heavier, more secure door for main rooms and entrances, while a lighter core suits stores and internal partitions. Confirm the leaf size, the frame it will hang in and the handing, and specify sturdy hinges and a dependable lockset. Finishes span flat white, matte colours and wood-grain to match your scheme. OfficeLand supplies flush PVC doors in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with measurement, fabrication and installation, handling offices, hostels, hospitals and estates in bulk. Tell us how many leaves you need and request a quote; we reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-wardrobes/' => 'Wardrobes and storage take a daily beating from damp, condensation and the humidity that hangs in Nigerian bedrooms, so the material they are built from decides how long they last. PVC and WPC wardrobes stay waterproof and termite-proof where chipboard and MDF units swell at the base, blow at the edges and sag once moisture creeps in. They wipe clean, never need repainting and keep clothing, linen and files in a dry, sealed environment, which matters as much in a store room or records office as in a bedroom. This section covers fitted wardrobes built to the exact run of a wall and sliding-door wardrobes that save floor space in tighter rooms. When planning, measure the full height, width and depth of the space, decide how to split hanging rails, shelves and drawers, and choose soft-close hinges or runners for a quieter, longer-lasting result. Finishes range from matte and gloss to wood-grain and marble-effect. OfficeLand supplies PVC wardrobes and storage in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring, fabricating and installing each unit, and we fit out hostels, hotels, estates and institutional projects in bulk. Share your room measurements and request a quote; our team replies within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-wardrobes/fitted-wardrobes/' => 'Fitted wardrobes make the most of a bedroom by building storage into the full height and width of a wall, turning awkward corners and alcoves into organised hanging, shelving and drawer space. Made in PVC and WPC, they bring that tailored look without the damp-related failures that plague timber and MDF built-ins in Nigeria, where humidity and the occasional leak swell panels, lift laminate and invite termites. These wardrobes are waterproof and termite-proof throughout, so the carcasses, shelves and doors all stay sound and easy to clean. Good planning starts with accurate measurements of the wall, floor to ceiling, allowing for skirting and any out-of-square walls. Decide the internal layout early: long hanging for dresses and coats, double hanging for shirts, plus shelves and drawers to suit the user. Soft-close hinges protect the doors and reduce slamming, and finishes from matte and gloss to wood-grain let the units blend with the room. OfficeLand supplies fitted PVC wardrobes in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with site measurement, fabrication and installation, and we handle multi-room developments, hotels and staff quarters in bulk. Send us your wall dimensions and request a quote, and we will respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-wardrobes/sliding-wardrobes/' => 'Sliding-door wardrobes are the practical answer where floor space is tight, because the doors glide along the face of the unit instead of swinging out into the room. That makes them a favourite for compact bedrooms, hostel rooms and apartments, and in PVC or WPC they add moisture resistance to that space-saving design. Unlike timber and chipboard sliders that swell and jam once humidity and damp reach them, PVC wardrobes stay waterproof and termite-proof, with doors that keep running smoothly for years. The heart of a good sliding wardrobe is its track and roller system, so look for sturdy top and bottom tracks and quality rollers, ideally with a soft-close action that stops the doors slamming. Measure the opening precisely, since sliding doors must overlap correctly to seal the interior, and plan the inside with hanging rails, shelves and drawers before fabrication. Finishes include mirror panels, wood-grain, matte and gloss to suit the room. OfficeLand supplies sliding-door PVC wardrobes in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring, fabricating and installing each one, and we fit out estates, hostels and institutional accommodation in volume. Give us your opening size and request a quote; we reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-kitchens/' => 'Kitchens are the wettest, hardest-working rooms in any building, which is why kitchen cabinetry built in PVC and WPC makes so much sense in Nigeria. Spills, steam, washing-up water and humidity ruin timber, chipboard and MDF carcasses in a few seasons, swelling the base units nearest the sink and lifting laminate at every edge, while termites finish the job out of sight. PVC and WPC cabinetry is 100% waterproof and termite-proof throughout the carcass and doors, so it stays solid under the sink, wipes clean of grease and never needs repainting. This section covers base and wall cabinets as well as islands and worktop units. When planning, set the layout around the sink, cooker and fridge, confirm ceiling height for tall units, and choose soft-close hinges and drawer runners that survive constant use. Finishes run from high-gloss and matte to wood-grain and marble-effect fronts. OfficeLand supplies PVC kitchen cabinetry in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with professional measurement, fabrication and installation, and we handle complete kitchens for homes, estates, hotels and institutional catering in bulk. Send us your kitchen layout or drawings and request a quote; our team responds within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-kitchens/kitchen-cabinets/' => 'Kitchen cabinets carry the daily load of a Nigerian kitchen, from heavy pots in the base units to crockery in the wall cabinets, all in an atmosphere of steam, grease and humidity. PVC and WPC cabinets handle that far better than wooden or chipboard units, which swell, delaminate and rot once water reaches them under the sink and along the splashback. Being fully waterproof and termite-proof, PVC carcasses and doors stay square and sound, wipe clean of cooking grime and never need repainting. When specifying, separate base cabinets from wall cabinets and allow for the worktop depth and the gap for the splashback, then plan drawers where you want pots and utensils and shelves where you want crockery. Soft-close hinges and full-extension drawer runners make a noticeable difference to how the kitchen feels and lasts. Door finishes include gloss, matte and wood-grain to match the scheme. OfficeLand supplies PVC kitchen cabinets in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring, fabricating and installing each run, and we fit out apartments, estates and institutional kitchens in bulk. Share your wall lengths and appliance positions and request a quote, and we will reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-kitchens/kitchen-islands/' => 'An island or freestanding worktop unit gives a kitchen extra preparation surface, storage and a natural place to gather, and in PVC or WPC it brings that function without the moisture problems of a timber-framed island. Standing in the open, often near the sink or hob, an island meets splashes and humidity on every side, so a waterproof, termite-proof carcass is exactly what keeps it solid and clean for the long term. These units never swell, rot or need repainting, and they wipe down easily after cooking. Planning an island starts with clearance: leave enough room to walk and open doors all the way round, usually around a metre, and make sure the island suits the overall kitchen layout rather than crowding it. Decide how to use the base, whether as drawers, cabinets, open shelving or a mix, and choose soft-close hardware for everyday comfort. Finishes can match or deliberately contrast the main run, in gloss, matte, wood-grain or marble-effect. OfficeLand supplies PVC kitchen islands and worktop units in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with measurement, fabrication and installation, handling homes, show kitchens and institutional projects in bulk. Tell us your kitchen size and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-interiors/' => 'Decorative wall and ceiling panels are a fast, clean way to transform the look of a room while sealing surfaces against Nigeria\'s damp. Where paint peels and plaster blooms with mould in humid, leak-prone buildings, PVC panels go straight over blockwork, old plaster or tired ceilings to give a crisp, washable finish in a day or two, with far less mess than wet trades. They are waterproof, termite-proof and wipe clean, which makes them equally at home in living rooms, offices, shops, bathrooms and reception areas. This section covers both wall panels and ceiling panels, so you can treat a single feature wall or wrap a whole room. When planning, measure the surface area to work out panel quantities, choose a finish such as wood-grain, marble-effect, matte or gloss, and allow for matching trims to close internal and external corners neatly. Because panels are light and interlocking, installation is quick and needs minimal sub-structure. OfficeLand supplies PVC wall and ceiling panels in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with measurement, supply and professional installation, and we take on full interior fit-outs, commercial spaces and institutional projects in bulk. Send us your room sizes and request a quote; our team replies within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-interiors/wall-panels/' => 'PVC wall panels give walls a smart, uniform finish without the recurring battle of painting, patching and treating mould that plagues painted plaster in Nigeria\'s humid, damp-prone climate. They fix directly over existing walls, hiding cracks and uneven plaster behind a flat, washable surface, and because they are fully waterproof they suit bathrooms, kitchens, shops and reception walls as readily as living rooms and offices. The panels are termite-proof, wipe clean with a cloth and never need repainting, so a feature wall still looks fresh years later. When ordering, measure the height and width of each wall to calculate panel runs, and decide on a finish, whether a warm wood-grain, a cool marble-effect, or a plain matte or gloss colour, to set the mood of the room. Plan for trims at corners, skirtings and where panels meet doors and windows, as these give the installation its tidy, deliberate edges. The panels are light and interlock quickly on a simple framework. OfficeLand supplies PVC wall panels in Lagos and delivers nationwide, measuring, supplying and installing them, and we handle offices, hotels, shops and institutional interiors in bulk. Share your wall measurements and request a quote; we will respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-interiors/ceiling-panels/' => 'Ceilings suffer first when a roof leaks or humidity builds up, and in Nigeria that means stained, sagging POP and asbestos-era boards or warped timber ceilings. PVC ceiling panels avoid all of this: being waterproof and termite-proof, they resist water marks, do not rot or host mould, and keep a clean, bright finish overhead for years. They are light, so they install quickly on a modest grid or furring, and they wipe clean if dust or kitchen grease settles, which suits homes, offices, shops, bathrooms and canteens alike. When planning a ceiling, measure the room area carefully to work out panel quantities and the direction of the runs, and consider where lights, fans and air-conditioning outlets fall so panels can be cut neatly around them. Choose a finish, from clean matte white to wood-grain or marble-effect, and allow for matching perimeter trims to frame the ceiling against the walls. OfficeLand supplies PVC ceiling panels in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with measurement, supply and professional installation, and we take on whole-building ceilings for estates, offices, schools and institutional projects in bulk. Tell us your ceiling dimensions and request a quote, and our team will reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-boards/' => 'PVC boards and sheets are the raw material behind durable, waterproof interiors, used for everything from cabinet carcasses and shelving to wall cladding, signage, partitions and bespoke furniture. For fabricators, carpenters and developers working in Nigeria, they replace plywood, MDF and particleboard that fail fast in damp, flood-prone and termite-infested conditions, offering a stable, waterproof, termite-proof substrate that cuts, routs, screws and glues much like timber but never swells or rots. This section brings together flat boards and sheets in a range of thicknesses, along with the edging and trims that finish cut edges cleanly. When ordering, the critical choice is thickness: thinner sheets suit cladding, panelling and light duties, while thicker boards carry the structural load of cabinets, worktop supports and shelving that must not sag. Consider the density and surface finish too, depending on whether the board will be seen, laminated or hidden. OfficeLand supplies PVC boards and sheets in Lagos and delivers nationwide, cutting to size where needed, and we supply workshops, furniture makers, contractors and institutional projects in bulk, including tenders and government work. Send us your board sizes and quantities and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-boards/pvc-sheets/' => 'Flat PVC boards and sheets are the workhorse material for anyone building moisture-proof interiors, from kitchen and wardrobe carcasses to wall cladding, display units, partitions and signage. In Nigeria, where plywood delaminates, MDF crumbles and particleboard disintegrates once damp, flooding or termites take hold, these sheets give fabricators a waterproof, termite-proof base that stays flat and stable. They machine like timber, taking screws, routing and adhesives well, yet never swell, warp or need treating. The first decision when ordering is thickness, matched to the job: lighter sheets for cladding, backing and panelling, and heavier boards for cabinet bodies, shelves and anything that must bear weight without bowing over a span. Think about the sheet size against your cutting plan to minimise waste, and whether you need a plain or foamed board depending on weight and finish. Pair the sheets with suitable edging to seal and tidy the cut edges. OfficeLand supplies PVC boards and sheets in Lagos and delivers nationwide, cutting to size on request, and we supply furniture workshops, shopfitters, contractors and institutional and government projects in bulk. Give us your sheet sizes, thicknesses and quantities and request a quote, and we will reply within four working hours.',

    '/pvc-doors-interiors/pvc-boards/pvc-edging/' => 'Edging and trims are the finishing touch that turn raw PVC board into a clean, professional piece of work, sealing cut edges and covering the joints where panels, boards and surfaces meet. Without them, exposed board edges look unfinished and can let moisture creep into the core over time, which matters even with waterproof PVC in Nigeria\'s humid interiors. Edge banding caps the visible sides of cabinets, shelves and worktops, while profile trims close internal and external corners, frame wall and ceiling panels, and neaten the line where cladding meets doors, windows and skirtings. When ordering, match the edging width to the board thickness so it wraps fully, and pick a colour or finish that matches or deliberately contrasts the panel, from white and wood-grain to marble-effect and gloss. Choose the right trim profile for each junction, since corner, end and joining pieces each do a different job. These accessories are light and quick to apply, and they lift the quality of the whole installation. OfficeLand supplies PVC edging and trims in Lagos and delivers nationwide, and we supply fabricators, fit-out contractors and institutional projects in bulk to match their boards and panels. Send us your profiles and quantities and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',
